we are now less than three weeks away  from apple's rumored march 8th spring  event where they're expected to release  a bunch of new products including a new  iphone se three new mac models and of  course the ipad air 5. so what i'm going  to be doing in this video is going  through all of the final leaks and  rumors as well as my own reasoning for  why i'm 100 sure we'll be seeing a new  ipad air at this event and then i'll  explain why our ipad air 5 custom  renders have a square camera bump on  them but before i get into all of the  main leaks that really solidify the  rumors of the ipad air coming at next  month's events i want to first go  through the logical and common sense  approach to why it makes sense for it to  come as soon as possible so let's get  right into it last year in september  apple revealed the new ipad mini 6 which  came with a full redesign finally  matching the modern design of the ipad  air and the ipad pro complete with the  usb c port but the thing i didn't expect  apple to do was to go above and beyond  with the new ipad mini specifically by  giving it the brand new a15 bionic chip  instead of sticking to the a14 and the  reason this was so shocking to me was  because the ipad air 4 that is currently  still up for sale comes with the older  a14 chip while actually being a hundred  dollars more expensive than the new mini  with the a15 chip to me this makes  absolutely no sense at all for a less  expensive ipad to come with a newer and  faster chip which puts the entire lineup  into disarray but wait that is not the  only problem the ipad mini 6 has a bunch  of other advantages over the ipad air  like for example it comes with a much  better camera system it actually gets a  flash module while the air does not and  it comes with upgraded video recording  capabilities like getting cinematic  video stabilization at 4k resolution and  it gets extended dynamic range at up to  30 fps while the air doesn't get it at  all but the absolutely biggest  difference is that the new mini comes  with the brand new 12 megapixel ultra  wide selfie camera with features like  lens correction smart hdr3 extended  dynamic range and stabilization which is  a huge step above the basic 7 megapixel  camera on the air and it comes with the  center stage feature for facetime video  and believe it or not even the new  budget ipad for only 329  gets this new 12 megapixel ultrawide  camera as well which makes it even more  obvious that the current ipad air 4  makes literally no sense right now in  the current ipad lineup and on top of  that the new ipad mini 6 actually  supports 5g connectivity which is  obviously extremely important to apple  and the ipad air of course does not have  that right now so in my opinion apple  needs to fix this messed up ipad lineup  asap which is why they absolutely need  to release the ipad air 5 at the next  possible event which should be on march  8th but beyond that there is actually  even more common sense evidence for why  apple should be releasing this ipad air  at their upcoming spring event instead  of later in the year ever since 2019 the  ipad air has been on a 1.5 year release  cycle with the current ipad air 4 being  released in september of 2020 which  would point to a spring 2022 release  date a year and a half later but an even  more important point i want to make is  that the ipad air has never been  released in the middle of the year or in  the summer time and it has also never  been released alongside the ipad pro and  this makes total sense because the ipad  air and the pro are right next to each  other in the lineup currently being  fairly similar in terms of the design  and only a couple of hundred dollars  apart in terms of the price point so it  would kind of create a conflict of  attention but if you've been following  the rumors for the upcoming m2 ipad pro  you'll know that basically all the  rumors are pointing to it coming in the  fall including mark german who is hands  down the most reliable leaker as well as  dylan dkt who said it's coming in the  fall for sure and i personally agree  with this because i believe apple has to  debut the new m2 chip on a mac first  before giving it to the ipad pro later  which is exactly what they did with the  previous m1 ipad pro and finally the  ipad pro has mostly also been on a 1.5  year update cycle just like the ipad air  with the exception of last year with the  whole m1 chip launch and i believe  they're going to go back on that 1.5  year cycle again pointing to a fall  release for the new ipad pro and the  whole point i'm trying to make is that  it means that the ipad air absolutely  needs to get released this spring to  avoid being released alongside the ipad  pro in the fall which apple has never  done before and i don't think they will  so with that said let's move on to all  the latest leaks and rumors that confirm  this theory as well as the new features  and changes that we should expect  but first i've got to show you guys our  new ipad air 5 renders in the green  aluminum finish alongside this beautiful  green wallpaper which you can find a  download link to in the video  description below and yes the design  looks extremely familiar apart from one  noticeable difference the camera bomb  now getting into the leaks for many  months it was believed that the ipad air  would be the first ipad to come with an  oled display but that was apparently  delayed until 2023  according to ross young and shortly  after that major quote agreed and said  that the 2022 ipad air will be sticking  to the same lcd display that we  currently have which is a bit  disappointing but then in july of last  year mac osakara gave us a massive  report in terms of what to expect from  the design and in the report they claim  that the overall design will remain  unchanged with the same 10.9 inch  display and the same touch id power  button but that it would gain a dual  lens camera system with both wide and  ultra wide cameras which is exactly what  we have on the current ipad pro and in  my opinion this makes total sense  because apple's magic keyboard supports  both the ipad air and the ipad pro but  on the air it looks a bit weird because  the singular camera bump doesn't really  fit in the squarish hole in the case and  that is exactly why our new renders come  with a dual lens square bump complete  with a flash and a microphone hole  perfectly matching the iphone 13 camera  bump design and you might also notice  that the lidar scanner is missing  because mac otakara couldn't confirm if  it was coming or not and i think it  makes sense to keep it exclusive to the  ipad pro models for at least another  year now apart from that they also  believe that the new ipad air will get a  four speaker audio system instead of the  current two speaker system and this  makes total sense to me because it  already has the four speaker grilles and  it's expected to slowly gain ipad pro  features over the years they also  believe that it'll get an upgrade to the  a15 chip which is a very obvious change  that i can guarantee will happen along  with everything else that the ipad mini  received last year like optional 5g  connectivity camera performance updates  and of course the new 12 megapixel ultra  wide selfie camera but other than that i  honestly don't think it'll be getting  anything else with the three major  feature changes being the new squarish  camera bump the a15 chip and the quad  stereo speakers which is why i believe  it'll still be carrying the same price  of  599 dollars as the current model is and  now finally let's finish off with the  major leaks that confirm that the ipad  air will be revealed at apple's spring  event last month apple registered new  ipad model numbers with the eec that are  likely for the new ipad air 5 and mark  gurman basically confirmed this recently  by flat out saying that apple plans to  unveil the new ipad air at the march 8th  event which is the biggest confirmation  yet and mac atakara also came back and  even confirmed that the new ipad air  models have actually entered mass  production ahead of the event so if we  combine all of those leaks alongside the  fact that the ipad air desperately needs  an update in order to make it make sense  within the ipad lineup as well as being  on a 1.5 year update cycle i can  confidently say that the ipad air will  be revealed at apple's upcoming spring  event 100 confirmed no doubt about it  now if you disagree with me then go  ahead and let me know in the comment  section below but if you enjoyed this  video click that circle about to  subscribe for more videos like this one  and check out that video which talks  about the max that we're expecting at  the march event thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

